The proposed the Street Vendors (Protection of Livelihood and Regulation of Street Vending) Bill, 2012, inter alia, seeks to provide for the following,
namely:-
a. Compulsory registration of every person intending to carry out street vending activities. b. Issue of a certificate of vending and identity cards to street vendors;
c. Certain rights of street vendors; d.Certain duties of the street vendors; e.
Constitution of Town Vending Committee in each local authority with minimum forty per cent representation of street vendors, out of which, one-third shall be women vendors and reasonable representation of the Scheduled Castes, the Scheduled Tribes, Other Backward Classes, minorities and persons with disabilities; f. Making of a plan for street vending once in every five years;
g. Framing of a scheme relating to street vending by the appropriate Government;
h. Redressal of grievances and resolution of disputes of street vendors;
i. Promotional measures for making available credit, insurance and other welfare schemes of social security for the street vendors;
j. Street vendors not to be prevented by any person or police or any other authority from exercising their right KL,J to vend when carrying on street vending in accordance with the terms and conditions of certificate of vending."
